# Commercial S8.3 transport resilience

## Ausgangslage

The strict S8.2 two-hour public observation was rolled back safely to S7 after
two isolated, retryable `S8_TELEGRAM_API_UNAVAILABLE` polling failures. Service,
resource, proxy, database and product-boundary evidence remained green. The
failure therefore demonstrated an overly strict transport gate rather than a
product-boundary or S7 stability failure.

The verified recovery baseline remains:

`/opt/tu1nz_repos/backups/commercial-s8-public-telegram/20260830T172823Z-pre-public-activation`

with index SHA-256:

`9084222f4fceff61afe254999312f3c212c57d2785a67a8aa2f9d7ceb1ee08b3`

No schema or durable-data change is part of S8.3. The existing baseline plus the
exact Git release SHAs are therefore the approved rollback basis for the
reversible staging delta.

## S8.3 policy

- Retryable Telegram timeout/connection/5xx and rate-limit failures are YELLOW
  inside a rolling 8-failure/15-minute budget.
- Retry uses 1-to-60-second bounded exponential backoff, up to one second of
  jitter and a bounded provider `Retry-After`.
- Three consecutive failures open the circuit for 30 seconds; a half-open probe
  controls recovery.
- The ninth failure inside the rolling window is RED.
- Auth, identity, group, webhook, command and contract failures are immediately
  RED.
- Safety exit status 2 is not restarted by systemd.
- Runtime health uses the fresh poll heartbeat and performs no separate long
  Telegram request. Prestart remains a strict remote identity check.
- Stale notification `SENDING` leases become terminal outcome-uncertain records
  and are never automatically replayed because Telegram offers no caller
  idempotency key for `sendMessage`.
- S7 remains active and the nginx backup upstream throughout staging and public
  observation.

## Acceptance gate

Offline application acceptance is GREEN with 819/819 tests, deterministic fault
injection, compile validation, JSON validation and a clean secret scan. The
observer now permits at most two temporary YELLOW health samples and at most
eight verified retryable transport failures, while still requiring a GREEN final
sample, zero RED events, zero restarts, stable S7/S8/landing/nginx processes,
closed Adult/AVS/payment/publishing boundaries and clean exact repositories.

Server re-acceptance remains a bounded STOP -> INSTALL -> VERIFY -> START ->
OBSERVE flow. Any hard failure or exhausted budget is fail-closed and uses the
versioned S8-to-S7 rollback. No Adult media, AVS, payment, publishing, creator
invite, controlled beta or production workflow is authorized.

The canonical Application integration is merge commit
`c82ad7daa0409cea0719f9749872d9c3e2f193fc` with tree
`fa89f12c0eef27422997d17acad43260677df979` and parents
`935518614d4e9e6ce302c75bf81d6e5ca2a4f1d4` and
`dc1ababa277d975829eef3894211cc52caaa6841`. Control binds the server sync to
that canonical merge commit, not to a feature-branch-only SHA.
